  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **ween2003-07-29d1t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2003-07-29.akg463** (recommended): source not stated; 31 songs; 147 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **ween-2003-07-29.mk-4v.sxm-2.sbm-1.d-100**: source not stated; 0 songs; 152 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Deaner's tour diary says Ween played a two-night stand at First Avenue, a club they like and have played countless times [1]\n- Ween also played an in-store at Electric Fetus Records, with nearly 500 people packed in a hot store; rented gear malfunctioned and scrapped the planned Quebec songs [1]\n- The show was sold out; the reviewer waited over two hours outside before a stranger handed him a ticket just as it began [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2003-07-29.akg463**: taped by Steve Pzynski; transferred by Al Angen; source: FOB: AKG 463 [Jim Williams mod] > GP DMIC-20 > D100 [Oade mod.] [1]. Also: Uploader adjusted where songs start and end, which he says improved the sound of the recording [1]",
